# busybox init. Three things, and the order matters.
#
# sysinit runs to completion BEFORE any respawn entry starts, so anything that
# blocks in rcS costs you every way back into the device -- both the serial
# console and the network shell are respawn entries below.
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS

# No telnet: ssh (dropbear) is the only network login. The trial boot and
# its self-revert are the way back if ssh ever fails to come up.
ttyS0::respawn:/bin/login -p

::restart:/sbin/init
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
